{
  "title": "47: Muhammad محمد",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاَلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَصَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ اَضَلَّ اَعْمَالَهُمْ‏(1)\nLAZEENA KAFAROO WASADDOOA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE AZALLAL A-A’MAALAHUM.\nThose who disbelieve and hinder (others) from the Path of God, He shall render in vain their deeds\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَاٰمَنُوْا بِمَا نُزِّلَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّهُوَ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّهِمْ‌ۙ كَفَّرَ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّاٰتِهِمْ وَاَصْلَحَ بَالَهُمْ‏(2)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WA AAMANOO BEMAA NUZZELA A’LAA MUHAMMADIN WA HAQQO MIN RABBEHIM KAFFARA A’NHUM SAYYEAATEHIM WAASLAHA BAALAHUM.\nAnd those who believe and do good, and believe in what hath been sent down unto (Our Apostle) Muhammad, and (that) it is the truth from their Lord, He will remove from them their evils, and (shall) improve their state.\nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا اتَّبَعُوا الْبَاطِلَ وَاَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اتَّبَعُوا الْحَقَّ مِنْ رَّبِّهِمْ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يَضْرِبُ اللّٰهُ لِلنَّاسِ اَمْثَالَهُمْ‏(3)\nZAA LEKA BE-ANNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO ATTABAU’OOA AL-BAATELA WA ANNAL LAZEENA AAMANUT ATTABAU’OOA HAQQA MIN RABBEHIM KAZAALEKA YAZREBU LAAHO LIN-NAASE AMSAALAHUM.\nThat is because, those who disbelieve follow falsehood, and those who believe follow the truth from their Lord; Thus doth God set forth unto the people their examples.\nفَاِذَا لَقِيْتُمُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فَضَرْبَ الرِّقَابِ ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَاۤ اَثْخَنْتُمُوْهُمْ فَشُدُّوْا الْوَثَاقَ ۙ فَاِمَّا مَنًّۢا بَعْدُ وَاِمَّا فِدَآءً حَتّٰى تَضَعَ الْحَرْبُ اَوْزَارَهَا ۛۚ  ذٰ لِكَ ‌ۛؕ وَلَوْ يَشَآءُ اللّٰهُ لَانْتَصَرَ مِنْهُمْ  وَلٰكِنْ لِّيَبْلُوَا۟ بَعْضَكُمْ بِبَعْضٍ‌ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ قُتِلُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ فَلَنْ يُّضِلَّ اَعْمَالَهُمْ‏(4)\nFA-EZAA LAQEETUMU LAZEENA KAFAROO FAZARBA FIR REQAAB HATTAA EZAA AASKHANTUMOOHUM FASHUDDOOA AL-WASAAQA FA-IMMAA MANNAW BA’DO WA AMMAA FEDAAAN HATTAA TAZAA’A AL-HARBU AAWZAARAHAA ZAA LEKA WA LAW YASHAAA LAAHO LAANTASARA MINHUM WA LAAKIL LLEEBLOOA BAA’ZAKUM BE-BA’Z WA WAL LAZEENA QUTELOOA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE FALAN YYUZELLA A-A’MAALAHUM.\nSo when ye encounter those who disbelieve (in a battle) then smite the necks until when ye have routed wounding them (rendering them helpless) and take them captives, under fetters, or set them free as an obligation or they be ransomed, until they lay down the weapons; Thus (are ye commanded); and if God be pleased, certainly would He exact retribution from them, but rather He would try some of you through the others; And those who are slain in the way of God, never will He allow their deeds to go in vain.\nسَيَهْدِيْهِمْ وَيُصْلِحُ بَالَهُمْۚ‏(5)\nSAYAHDEEHEM WAYUSLEHU BAALAHUM.\nSoon will He guide them aright and improve their state;\nوَيُدْخِلُهُمُ الْجَنَّةَ عَرَّفَهَا لَهُمْ‏(6)\nWAYUDKHELUHUMU JANNATA A’ARRAFAHAA LAHUM.\nAnd admit them to the garden which He hath made known to them.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنْ تَنْصُرُوا اللّٰهَ يَنْصُرْكُمْ وَيُثَبِّتْ اَقْدَامَكُمْ‏(7)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO IN TANSUROOA LAAHA YANSURKUM WAYUSABBET AAQDAAMAKUM.\nO’ ye who believe if ye help (in the way of) God, He will (also) help you, and will set firm your feet.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فَتَعْسًا لَّهُمْ وَاَضَلَّ اَعْمَالَهُمْ‏(8)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO FATAA’SAN LAHUM WA AZALLAL A-A’MAALAHUM.\nAnd those who disbelieve, stumbling (with destruction) shall be for them, and He shall render (all) their (good) deeds in vain.\nذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَرِهُوْا مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ فَاَحْبَطَ اَعْمَالَهُمْ‏(9)\nZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM KAREHOOA MAA ANZALAL LAAHO FAAHBATA A-A’MAALAHUM.\nThat is for they hated what God sent down, so shall He render null their deeds.\nاَفَلَمْ يَسِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَيَنْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ‌ؕ دَمَّرَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ اَمْثَالُهَا‏(10)\nA-FALAM YASEEROO FIL ARZE FAYANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM DAMMARA LAAHO A’LAYHIM WA LIL KAAFEREENA AAMSAALUHAA.\nWhat! have they not travelled in the earth and seen how was the end of those before them? God brought destruction on them, and for the disbelievers shall be the like unto it.\nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّ اللّٰهَ مَوْلَى الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَاَنَّ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ لَا مَوْلٰى لَهُمْ‏(11)\nZAA LEKA BE-ANNAL LAAHA MAWLAA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA ANNAL KAAFEREEN LAA MAWLAA LAHUM.\nThat is for God is the guardian of those who believe, and that the infidels, there shall not be any guardian for them.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُدْخِلُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ‌ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يَتَمَتَّعُوْنَ وَيَاْكُلُوْنَ كَمَا تَاْكُلُ الْاَنْعَامُ وَالنَّارُ مَثْوًى لَّهُمْ‏(12)\nINNAL LAAHA YUDKHELU LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO WAL LAZEENA KAFAROO YATAMATTAU’OONA WA YAAKOLOON KAMAA TAAKULU AL-AANA’AAMU WA TAMASSANAN MASWAL LAHUM.\nVerily, God will admit those who believe and do good, to the gardens ’neath which flow rivers; and those who disbelieve enjoy themselves and eat as the beasts eat, and the fire shall be their abode.\nوَكَاَيِّنْ مِّنْ قَرْيَةٍ هِىَ اَشَدُّ قُوَّةً مِّنْ قَرْيَتِكَ الَّتِىْۤ اَخْرَجَتْكَ‌ۚ اَهْلَكْنٰهُمْ فَلَا نَاصِرَ لَهُمْ‏(13)\nWA KA-AYYIM MIN QARYATINW HEYA ASHADDO QUWWAH MIN QARYATEKA LATEE AAKHRAJATKA AHLAKNAAHUM FALAA NAASERA LAHUM.\nAnd how many a town which was mightier in power than thy town which hath driven thee out; We destroyed them, and no helper was there for them.\nاَفَمَنْ كَانَ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖ كَمَنْ زُيِّنَ لَهٗ سُوْٓءُ عَمَلِهٖ وَاتَّبَعُوْۤا اَهْوَآءَهُمْ‏(14)\nAFAMAWN KAANA A’LAA BAYYENAH MIN RABBEHI KAMAM ZUYYENA LAHU SOOO-UL A’AMALEH WAT TABA-O’O AHWAAA-AHUM.\nWhat! is he who is on (the path of the) clear proofs from his Lord like unto him whom the evil of his work is made fairseeming; and follow they their (own) vain desires?\nمَثَلُ الْجَنَّةِ الَّتِىْ وُعِدَ الْمُتَّقُوْنَ‌ؕ فِيْهَاۤ اَنْهٰرٌ مِّنْ مَّآءٍ غَيْرِ اٰسِنٍ‌ ۚ وَاَنْهٰرٌ مِّنْ لَّبَنٍ لَّمْ يَتَغَيَّرْ طَعْمُهٗ ‌ۚ وَاَنْهٰرٌ مِّنْ خَمْرٍ لَّذَّةٍ لِّلشّٰرِبِيْنَ ۚ وَاَنْهٰرٌ مِّنْ عَسَلٍ مُّصَفًّى‌ ؕ وَلَهُمْ فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلِّ الثَّمَرٰتِ وَمَغْفِرَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمْ‌ؕ كَمَنْ هُوَ خَالِدٌ فِى النَّارِ وَسُقُوْا مَآءً حَمِيْمًا فَقَطَّعَ اَمْعَآءَهُمْ‏(15)\nMASALUL JANNAH LATEE WUE’EDA AL-MUTTAQOONA FEEHAA AANHAARUN MIN MAAA-IN GHAIRE AAASENIN WAANHAARUN MIN LLABANIN LAM YATAGHAYR TAA’MUH WAANHAARUN MIN KHAMRIN LLAZZATIN LLELSSHAAREBEENA WAANHAARUN MIN A’ASALIN MMUSAFFAN WA LAHUM FEEHAA MIN KULLE SAMARAATE WAMAGHFERATUN MIN RABBEHIM KAMAM HOWA KHAALEDUN FIL NAAR WASUQOOA MAAA-AN HAMEEMANW FAQATTAA’A AAMA’AAAHUM.\nA similitude of the garden which has been promised to the pious ones. Therein are rivers of water incorruptible, and rivers of milk, changeth not its taste, and rivers of wine – delicious unto those who drink, and rivers of honey pure and clear; And for them therein are (all kinds) of fruits and (a total) forgiveness from their Lord; (can these be) Like unto those who shall dwell in the fire? and who shall be made to drink boiling water so that it will rend asunder their bowels.\nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّسْتَمِعُ اِلَيْكَ‌ۚ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا خَرَجُوْا مِنْ عِنْدِكَ قَالُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ مَاذَا قَالَ اٰنِفًا‌‌ اُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ طَبَعَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ وَ اتَّبَعُوْۤا اَهْوَآءَهُمْ‏(16)\nWA MINHUM MAN YYASTAMEU’U ELAYKA HATTAA EZAA KHARAJOO MIN I’NDEK QAALOO LILLAZEENA OOTUL OOTUL I’LMA MAA QAALA AAANEFAN OOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA TABAA’A LAAHO A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM WA TABA-O’O WA AHWAAA-AHUM.\nAnd of them are those who seek to listen to thee until when they go forth from thee say they unto those who have been given the knowledge: “What was it that he said just now?” These are they on whose hearts hath God set a seal, and follow they their vain desires.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اهْتَدَوْا زَادَهُمْ هُدًى وَّاٰتٰٮهُمْ تَقْوٰٮهُمْ‏(17)\nWAL LAZEENA TADAW ZAADAHUM HODAM WWAATAAHUM TAQWAAHUM.\nAnd those who avail of the guidance, He addeth to His guidance unto them, and granteth them their guard (against evils)\nفَهَلْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَّا السَّاعَةَ اَنْ تَاْتِيَهُمْ بَغْتَةً ‌ ۚ فَقَدْ جَآءَ اَشْرَاطُهَا‌‌ ۚ فَاَنّٰى لَهُمْ اِذَا جَآءَتْهُمْ ذِكْرٰٮهُمْ‏(18)\nFA HAL YANZOROONA ILLAA SAA-A’TA AN TAATEEHUM BAGHTATANW FAQAD JAAA-A AASHRAATUHAA FA-ANNAA LAHUM EZAA JAAA-AHUM ZEKRAAHUM.\nWhat! wait they then for aught save the Hour (of Reckoning) that it cometh on them all of a sudden? Indeed have (already) come the signs of it; and of what avail can be the reminder to them when it hath already come on them?\nفَاعْلَمْ اَنَّهٗ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَاسْتَغْفِرْ لِذَنْۢبِكَ وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَ الْمُؤْمِنٰتِ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ مُتَقَلَّبَكُمْ وَمَثْوٰٮكُمْ‏(19)\nFAAA’LAM ANNAHU LAA ELAAHA ILLAA LAAHO WAASTAGHFER LE-ZAMBEKA LIL-MOAMENEENA WA WA MOAMENAATE WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO MUTAQALLABAKUM WAMASWAAKUM.\nSo know thou that there is no god but God, and seek thou protection for thy sins and for (the sins of) the believer men and believer women; and God knoweth well the place of your movements (in this world) and the place of your final rest (the hereafter).\nوَيَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَوْلَا نُزِّلَتْ سُوْرَةٌ ‌ۚ فَاِذَاۤ اُنْزِلَتْ سُوْرَةٌ مُّحْكَمَةٌ وَّذُكِرَ فِيْهَا الْقِتَالُ‌ۙ رَاَيْتَ الَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ يَّنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَيْكَ نَظَرَ الْمَغْشِىِّ عَلَيْهِ مِنَ الْمَوْتِ‌ؕ فَاَوْلٰى لَهُمْ‌ۚ‏(20)\nWA YAQOOLO LAZEENA AAMANOO LAWLAA NUZZELAT SOORATUN FA-EZAA UNZELAT SOORATUN MMUHKAMATUN WWAZUKERA FEEHAA QETAALO RA-AYTA LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN YYANZUROONA ELAYKA NAZARA AL-MAGHSHEAAAE A’LAYHE MENAL MAWT FAAWLAA LAHUM.\nAnd say those who believe: “Why hath not been sent a chapter (for us), “But when is sent down a decisive chapter, and mentioned therein is war, seest thou those in whose hearts is a disease look unto thee with a look of one on whom has fallen the shadow of death; woe unto them! far better will certainly be for them,\nطَاعَةٌ وَّقَوْلٌ مَّعْرُوْفٌ‌ فَاِذَا عَزَمَ الْاَمْرُ فَلَوْ صَدَقُوا اللّٰهَ لَكَانَ خَيْرًا لَّهُمْ‌ۚ‏(21)\nTAAA’ATUN WWAQAWLUN MA’ROOFUNW FA-EZAA A’AZAMA MIN FA LAW SADAQOOA LAAHA LAKAANA KHAYRAN LAHUM.\nObedience and a fair word; but when the affair is determined, then if they be true to God, it would certainly be better for them,\nفَهَلْ عَسَيْتُمْ اِنْ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ اَنْ تُفْسِدُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَتُقَطِّعُوْۤا اَرْحَامَكُمْ‏(22)\nFA HAL A’SAYTUM IN TAWALLAYTUM AN TUFSEDOO FIL ARZE WATUQATTEU’OOA AARHAAMAKUM.\nThen be like ye are, if ye hold authority, that ye make mischief in the earth and sever the ties of kinship!\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ لَعَنَهُمُ اللّٰهُ فَاَصَمَّهُمْ وَاَعْمٰٓى اَبْصَارَهُمْ‏(23)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA LA-A’NAHOMUL LAAHO FAASAMMAHUM WAAA’MAAA AABSAARAHUM.\nThose are they whom hath cursed God, and so hath he made them deaf and blinded their eyes.\nاَفَلَا يَتَدَبَّرُوْنَ الْقُرْاٰنَ اَمْ عَلٰى قُلُوْبٍ اَ قْفَالُهَا‏(24)\nAFALAA YATADABBAROONA QURAANA AM A’LAA QULOOBIN A’ZAABAN QFAALUHAA.\nWhat! Reflect they not on the Qur’an? Nay! on (their) hearts are (set) their locks.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ ارْتَدُّوْا عَلٰٓى اَدْبَارِهِمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الْهُدَى‌ۙ الشَّيْطٰنُ سَوَّلَ لَهُمْ ؕ وَاَمْلٰى لَهُمْ‏(25)\nINNAL LAZEENA ARTADDOOA A’LAA AADBAAREHEM MIN BA’DE MAA TABAYYANA LAHOMUL AL-HUDAA SHAYTAANO SAWLA LAHUM WAAMLAA LAHUM.\nVerily, those who return on the backs after hath become manifest unto them the guidance, the satan hath beguiled them, and hath given them a respite.\nذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ قَالُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ كَرِهُوْا مَا نَزَّلَ اللّٰهُ سَنُطِيْعُكُمْ فِىْ بَعْضِ الْاَمْرِۖۚ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ اِسْرَارَهُمْ‏(26)\nZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM QAALOO LILLAZEENA KAREHOOA MAA NAZZALAL LAAHO SANUTEEU’UKUM FEE BAA’ZE AL-AAMRE WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO AESRAARAHUM.\nThat is for they say unto those who hate what God hath sent down (saying): “We will obey you in a part of (this) matter” But God knoweth well their secret reservations.\nفَكَيْفَ اِذَا تَوَفَّتْهُمُ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ يَضْرِبُوْنَ وُجُوْهَهُمْ وَاَدْبَارَهُمْ‏(27)\nFA-KAYFA EZAA TAWAFFATHUMU TAHMELOHUL YAZREBOONA WUJOOHAHUM WAADBAARAHUM.\nBut how? When the angels causing them to die, will smite their faces and their backs.\nذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّهُمُ اتَّبَعُوْا مَاۤ اَسْخَطَ اللّٰهَ وَكَرِهُوْا رِضْوَانَهٗ فَاَحْبَطَ اَعْمَالَهُمْ‏(28)\nZAALEKA BEAANNAHUMU TABA-O’O WA MAA AASKHATA LAAHA WAKAREHOOA REZWAANAH FAAHBATA A-A’MAALAHUM.\nThat is for they follow what displeaseth God, and hate what is His pleasure, so hath He made null their deeds.\nاَمْ حَسِبَ الَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ اَنْ لَّنْ يُّخْرِجَ اللّٰهُ اَضْغَانَهُمْ‏(29)\nAM HASEBA LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN AN LAN-Y YYUKHREJA LAAHO AAZGHAANAHUM.\nOr deem those in whose hearts is a disease that never will God bring forth their spite?\nوَلَوْ نَشَآءُ لَاَرَيْنٰكَهُمْ فَلَعَرَفْتَهُمْ بِسِيْمٰهُمْ‌ؕ وَلَتَعْرِفَنَّهُمْ فِىْ لَحْنِ الْقَوْلِ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ اَعْمَالَكُمْ‏(30)\nWA LAW NASHAAA-O LAARAYNAAKAHUM FALAA’ARAFTAHUM BESEEMAAHUM WALATAA’REFANNAHUM FEE LAHNE AL-QAWLE WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO A-A’MAALAKUM.\nAnd if We willed We could certainly have shown them unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) and thou wouldst certainly have known them by their features; and (now) certainly thou (can) recognise them by the tone of (their) speech; and God knoweth well (all) your deeds.\nوَلَنَبْلُوَنَّكُمْ حَتّٰى نَعْلَمَ الْمُجٰهِدِيْنَ مِنْكُمْ وَالصّٰبِرِيْنَ ۙ وَنَبْلُوَا۟ اَخْبَارَكُمْ‏(31)\nWA LA-NABLOWANNAKUM HATTAA NAA’LAMA AL-MUJAAHEDEENA MINKUM WAS SAABEREENA WANABLOOA AAKHBAARAKUM.\nAnd certainly will We try you until We have known those who strive (fight) among you and the patient ones, and make your affairs known.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَصَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَشَآقُّوا الرَّسُوْلَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الْهُدٰىۙ لَنْ يَّضُرُّوا اللّٰهَ شَيْئًا ؕ وَسَيُحْبِطُ اَعْمَالَهُمْ‏(32)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WASADDOOA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE WA LAAHA YATTABE-U’R MIN BA’DE MAA TABAYYANA LAHOMUL HODAA LAN YYAZURROOA LAAHA SHAY-ANW WASAYUHBETU A-A’MAALAHUM.\nVerily, those who disbelieve and hinder (others) from the path of God, and oppose the Apostle after that the guidance hath been made manifest unto them, can never harm God in any way; and He will make null their deeds.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوا الرَّسُوْلَ وَلَا تُبْطِلُوْۤا اَعْمَالَكُمْ‏(33)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO AATEEU’OOA LAAHA WAATEEU’OOA YATTABE-U’R WA LAA TUBTELOO A-A’MAALAKUM.\nO’ ye who believe! Obey ye God, and obey ye the Apostle, and do not render null your deeds.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَصَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ مَاتُوْا وَهُمْ كُفَّارٌ فَلَنْ يَّغْفِرَ اللّٰهُ لَهُمْ‏(34)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WASADDOOA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE SUMMA MAATOOA WA HUM KUFFAARUN FALAN YAGHFERAL LAAHO LAHUM.\nVerily, those who disbelieve and hinder (others) from the way of God, then they die while they are disbelievers, then never will God forgive them.\nفَلَا تَهِنُوْا وَتَدْعُوْۤا اِلَى السَّلْمِ‌ۖ وَاَنْتُمُ الْاَعْلَوْنَ‌ۖ وَاللّٰهُ مَعَكُمْ وَلَنْ يَّتِرَكُمْ اَعْمَالَكُمْ‏(35)\nFALAA TAHENOOA WATADU’OOA ELAL AS-SALME WAANTUMU AL-AAA’LAWNA WAL LAAHO MA-A’KUM WA LAN YYATERAKUM A-A’MAALAKUM.\nSo be not fainthearted and call (the infidels) to peace, while ye have the upper hand, and God is with you, and never will He depreciate your deeds.\nاِنَّمَا الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا لَعِبٌ وَّلَهْوٌ‌ ؕ وَاِنْ تُؤْمِنُوْا وَتَتَّقُوْا يُؤْتِكُمْ اُجُوْرَكُمْ وَلَا يَسْئَلْكُمْ اَمْوَالَكُمْ‏(36)\nINNAMAA HAYAATUD DUNYAA LAE’EBUN WWALAHWUN WA LAM TOAMENOO WA TATTAQOO YUTEKUM AUJOORAKUM WA LAA YASALKUM AMWAALAKUM.\nThe life of this world is only an idle sport and a play, and if ye believe and guard (yourselves against evil ), He will give your recompense, and will ask not of you of your possessions.\nاِنْ يَّسْئَلْكُمُوْهَا فَيُحْفِكُمْ تَبْخَلُوْا وَيُخْرِجْ اَضْغَانَكُمْ‏(37)\nIN YYASALKUMOOHAA FAYUHFEKUM TABKHALOOA WA YUKHRIJ AAZGHAANAKUM.\nShould He ask them of you, and if He urgeth you, ye will be niggardly, and He will bring forth your spite.\nهٰۤاَنْتُمْ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ تُدْعَوْنَ لِتُنْفِقُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ‌ۚ فَمِنْكُمْ مَّنْ يَّبْخَلُ ‌ ۚ وَمَنْ يَّبْخَلْ فَاِنَّمَا يَبْخَلُ عَنْ نَّفْسِهٖ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ الْغَنِىُّ وَاَنْتُمُ الْفُقَرَآءُ ‌ۚ وَاِنْ تَتَوَلَّوْا يَسْتَبْدِلْ قَوْمًا غَيْرَكُمْ ۙ ثُمَّ لَا يَكُوْنُوْۤا اَمْثَالَكُم‏(38)\nHAANTUM HAAOOLAAA-E TUDA’AWNA LE-TUNFEQOO FEE SABEELIL LAAHE FA MINKUM MAN YYABKHALU WA MAN YYABKHAL FA-INNAMAA YABKHALU A’N NNAFSEH WAL LAAHO AL-GHANEAAAU WAANTUMU AL-FUQARAAU WA IN YASTABDEL QAWMAN GHAYRAKUM SUMMA LAA YAKOONOOA AAMSAALAKUM.\nLo! ye are they, who are called upon to spend in the way of God, but of you are those who are niggardly, and whosoever is niggardly, is niggardly only against his own self; and God is Self-Sufficient and ye are in need (of Him), and if ye turn back, He will bring in your place a people other than you, then they will not be like unto you.",
  "merits": "This is a ‘Madani’ Surah and it has 37 verses. In the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan it is narrated that the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that whoever recites this Surah will have his thirst quenched by the drink from the rivers of Jannah.\nImam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) said that the person who recites this Surah will never have doubts about his religion and will not fall into disbelief and Shirk. A thousand angels will send salutations to his grave after his death. He will be placed under the protection of Allah (s.w.t.) and His Prophet (s.a.w.a.). When the reciter of this Surah will arise from his grave, whichever way he turns, he will see the blessed face of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.).\nIf this Surah is written and kept as a talisman, it protects a person, whether he is asleep or awake, from all evils and problems. It is also a safety from insanity."
